class CadCommandSession(System.Object):
    """The command line of one document, as AutoCAD's: a command started by its name or alias, its prompts answered
    by points picked on the canvas, text typed, objects selected, Enter and Esc, with the history of what was
    asked and answered. It knows no window: the canvas and the command line call CadCommandSession.Feed,
    CadCommandSession.Feed, CadCommandSession.FeedSelection, CadCommandSession.Enter and
    CadCommandSession.Escape, and a test calls them the same way.

    The dialogs of AutoLISP's DCL functions: what shows them for this session.

    The object selection filter of FILTER, kept for the session as AutoCAD keeps its named filters.

    The AutoLISP of a document: the interpreter, the lines typed at the command line, the c: commands and load.

    What AutoLISP's command and vl-cmdf do in the session: each argument goes, in turn, to the command running or
    starts one, as typed (never as AutoLISP), the lines the command line would show are written when CMDECHO is
    1, and a PAUSE lets the user answer the prompt the command asks while the routine waits.

    A routine of AutoLISP that waits for the user: a get function, entsel or ssget asks, the evaluation returns
    to the session, and the question is asked as a prompt of a small command of its own, so that object snaps,
    typed points, the rubber band, transparent ZOOM and PAN and the refusal messages work as at any prompt. The
    answer resumes the routine, Esc gives it Function cancelled, and the command ends when the routine does.

    The point modifiers AutoCAD takes at any prompt for a point, typed or chosen from the Shift+right-click menu:
    FROM, a base point and an offset from it; M2P (MTP), the point midway between two; TT, a point tracking lines
    run from; TK (TRACKING), a point reached from another along the axes; and the point filters .X .Y .Z .XY .XZ
    .YZ, the coordinates named taken from one point and the rest from another.

    The answers typed at the prompts, which the Recent Input menu of the canvas offers again, as AutoCAD 2021's
    with its INPUTHISTORYMODE 15: those of every command of the session, kept apart by what the prompt asked, the
    points and numbers written in the drawing's units and the selection sets named by their count, \"Selection
    set (3 items)\".

    A distance or an angle asked with no base point and given by two points, as AutoCAD 2021 takes them: a point
    typed or picked at \"Enter new value for POLARDIST <0.0000>:\" asks \"Specify second point:\", a rubber band
    drawn from the first, and the distance between the two, or the direction from the first to the second,
    answers the prompt. 0,0 then 3,4 sets POLARDIST to 5; 0,0 then 1,1 sets SNAPANG to 45.

    The options of \"Select objects:\", as AutoCAD 2021's.

    PAN, ZOOM, CAL, SETVAR, the settings ORTHO, POLAR, OSNAP, GRID and SNAP, DIST, ID, LAYER, COLOR, LINETYPE,
    LWEIGHT, UNITS, QUICKCALC, DSETTINGS, TEXTSCR and the name of any system variable run inside another command,
    as AutoCAD 2021 runs 'PAN and 'ZOOM: typed with an apostrophe at any prompt but one for text, they ask their
    own prompts after \">>\", and once they end the command they interrupted writes \"Resuming LINE command.\"
    and asks its prompt again, the objects \"Select objects:\" gathered still gathered. One nests in the other,
    'ZOOM in a transparent PAN, as AutoCAD's does; 'ZOOM at ZOOM's own prompt is refused with ZOOM's words. A
    transparent CAL ends by typing its value at the prompt the command interrupted waits at, a point as 11,21,0
    or a distance as 7 (CadCommandContext.TransparentResult), as AutoCAD 2021 does.

    A point typed after an object snap override (END, MID, CEN typed, or chosen from the Shift+right-click menu),
    which AutoCAD 2021 takes as a click: the objects within the aperture of the point are looked at, and the snap
    point of any of them nearest the point is the answer, or \"No Endpoint found for specified point.\" and the
    prompt is asked again.

    The implied window of the Command prompt and of \"Select objects:\", as AutoCAD 2021's."""
    def __init__(self, document: CadDocument, registry: CadCommandRegistry = ...) -> None:
        """Makes the command line of a document."""
    @property
    def AngleOverride(self) -> float | None:
        """Gets the direction an angle override typed at the prompt holds the next point to, in radians
        counter-clockwise from the world's X axis; null where none was typed. <30 typed at a prompt for a point
        that has a base point, as LINE's next point, is AutoCAD's angle override: \"Angle Override: 30\" is
        written, the prompt is asked again, and a distance typed then runs along the line at 30 degrees, counted
