class CadLayerWalkRequest(System.Object):
    """The LayerWalk dialog of LAYWALK, as data its command and the window share: the layers listed, the filter that
    narrows them, the layers walked, and the choice to put the layers back as they were when it closes. Walking
    layers turns every layer but those selected off and thaws those selected, as AutoCAD's LayerWalk shows only
    the objects on the layers selected; with none selected every layer is as it was. A drawing of the layers
    WALL, DOOR and TRIM, walked on DOOR, shows the objects on DOOR alone; closed with Restore on exit, it has all
    three as they were. The changes are edits of the command's one undo step."""
